## 🛠️ Tech Stack

* **Python** (data processing, modeling)
* **BERT (Transformers)** – for mood and sentiment classification
* **Plotly / Dash** – for interactive visualizations
* **Pandas / NumPy** – for data manipulation
* **Jupyter / Streamlit** (optional) – for experiments and deployment

---

## 📂 Project Structure

```
📁 teen-mental-health-dashboard
│── data/                 # Input datasets (messages, logs, etc.)
│── notebooks/            # Model training & EDA
│── dashboard/            # Dashboard scripts
│── screenshots/          # Dashboard preview images
│── requirements.txt      # Python dependencies
│── app.py                # Main dashboard app
│── README.md             # Project documentation
```

---

## ⚡ Installation

1. Clone the repository

   ```bash
   git clone https://github.com/your-username/teen-mental-health-dashboard.git
   cd teen-mental-health-dashboard
   ```

2. Create a virtual environment & install dependencies

   ```bash
   pip install -r requirements.txt
   ```

3. Run the dashboard

   ```bash
   python app.py
   ```

4. Open your browser at `http://127.0.0.1:8050/`

---

## 📊 Data Sources

* **Messaging Data** (timestamp, app name, message count)
* **Mood Scores** generated using **BERT sentiment classification**
* **Derived Metrics** (overnight activity, risk scores, usage trends)

